<% content_for(:full_width, true) %>
<div class="tariffik-home">
  <section class="tf-hero tf-wrap" id="lookup" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
    <div class="tf-hero-copy">
      <p class="tf-eyebrow"><span class="tf-dot"></span> LESS PAPERWORK. MORE POSSIBILITY.</p>
      <h1 id="hero-title">Goodbye guesswork.<br>Hello, <span>commodity<br class="tf-desktop-break"> codes.</span></h1>
      <p class="tf-intro">That thing you’re importing? There’s a code for it.<br class="tf-desktop-break"> Find it with a product link, a little AI, and Tariffik.</p>
      <div class="tf-lookup" data-controller="lookup-limit"
           data-lookup-limit-authenticated-value="<%= user_signed_in? %>"
           data-lookup-limit-remaining-value="<%= @guest_lookups_remaining || 3 %>"
           data-lookup-limit-limit-reached-value="<%= (@guest_lookups_remaining || 3) <= 0 %>">
        <div data-lookup-limit-target="form" data-controller="lookup-progress">
          <%= form_with url: home_lookup_path, method: :post, data: { turbo_frame: "lookup_result", action: "submit->lookup-progress#submit" } do |f| %>
            <%= f.label :url, "Start with a product link", class: "tf-field-label" %>
            <div class="tf-input-row">
              <%= f.url_field :url, placeholder: "https://shop.com/your-product", required: true, class: "tf-url", autocomplete: "url", aria: { describedby: "lookup-help" } %>
              <button type="submit" data-lookup-progress-target="button" class="tf-button tf-button-primary">
                <span data-lookup-progress-target="buttonText">Find my code</span>
                <svg data-lookup-progress-target="spinner" class="hidden animate-spin size-4" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="3" opacity=".3"/><path d="M12 3a9 9 0 0 1 9 9" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="3"/></svg>
                <%= tf_arrow %>
              </button>
            </div>
            <div class="tf-lookup-help" id="lookup-help">
              <% unless user_signed_in? %>
                <span data-remaining-wrapper><strong data-lookup-limit-target="remaining"><%= @guest_lookups_remaining || 3 %></strong> free <span data-lookup-limit-target="lookupText"><%= (@guest_lookups_remaining || 3) == 1 ? 'lookup' : 'lookups' %></span> left · No account needed</span>
              <% else %>
                <%= link_to "View your dashboard →", dashboard_path %>
              <% end %>
            </div>
          <% end %>
        </div>
        <div class="hidden tf-limit" data-lookup-limit-target="limitReached">
          <p class="tf-eyebrow">KEEP THE GOOD THINGS COMING</p>
          <h2>Your next code is a sign-up away.</h2>
          <p>You’ve used your guest lookups. Get 5 lookups every month with a free account.</p>
          <%= link_to safe_join([ "Create free account ", tf_arrow ]), new_user_registration_path(source: "home_hero"), class: "tf-button tf-button-primary" %>
          <%= link_to "Sign in", new_user_session_path, class: "tf-text-link" %>
        </div>
        <%= turbo_frame_tag "lookup_result", class: "block no-loading-indicator", aria: { live: "polite" } %>
      </div>
      <p class="tf-photo-link">No link? <%= link_to "Look up a photo instead →", user_signed_in? ? new_product_lookup_path(tab: "photo") : new_user_registration_path(source: "home_photo") %> <span>Free account</span></p>
    </div>
    <div class="tf-hero-art" aria-label="Illustrative product classification">
      <div class="tf-art-header"><span>FROM PRODUCT TO PAPERWORK</span><span>01 / 03</span></div>
      <div class="tf-parcel" aria-hidden="true">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 400 270" fill="none"><path d="m65 85 148-60 132 65-145 68Z" fill="#e5c9a5" stroke="#3b332e" stroke-width="1.5"/><path d="m65 85 135 73v102L65 182Z" fill="#c8a57b" stroke="#3b332e" stroke-width="1.5"/><path d="m200 158 145-68v102l-145 68Z" fill="#ddba8f" stroke="#3b332e" stroke-width="1.5"/><path d="m122 62 137 68 27-13-137-66Z" fill="#f3e2c9"/><path d="m259 130 27-13v61l-27 13Z" fill="#ead4b4"/><path d="m87 124 69 38v53l-69-39Z" fill="#faf7ef"/><path d="m98 147 46 25m-46-14 33 18" stroke="#3b332e" stroke-width="2"/><path d="m98 171 3 2m4 2 1 1m4 2 3 2m4 2 2 1m4 2 1 1m4 2 3 2m4 2 2 1" stroke="#3b332e" stroke-width="12"/><path d="m302 189 0-25m-7 11 7-11 7 4m11 12v-25m-7 11 7-11 7 4" stroke="#3b332e" stroke-width="2"/></svg>
        <span class="tf-parcel-note">A little less<br>customs chaos.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="tf-sample">
        <div class="tf-sample-top"><span class="tf-eyebrow">EXAMPLE RESULT</span><span class="tf-status">✓ Suggested code</span></div>
        <div class="tf-sample-product"><span class="tf-shirt" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 48 48" fill="none"><path d="m15 8-11 8 7 9 5-3v19h16V22l5 3 7-9-11-8c-4 6-14 6-18 0Z" fill="#f8f6ef" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"/></svg></span><div><strong>Everyday cotton T-shirt</strong><p>Clothing / Knitted / Cotton</p></div></div>
        <div class="tf-code">6109 <span>10</span> 0010&nbsp;<%= tf_arrow(classes: "tf-code-arrow") %></div>
        <div class="tf-sample-bottom"><span>A code. And the reasoning behind it.</span><span class="tf-barcode" aria-hidden="true"></span></div>
      </div>
      <p class="tf-art-footnote">Illustrative result. Always review your suggested classification.</p>
      <span class="tf-art-cross" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="tf-trust"><div class="tf-wrap"><p>MADE FOR IMPORTS TO THE<br><strong>UK & Channel Islands</strong></p><span>Official UK tariff data</span><span>AI-powered suggestions</span><span>Clear, human explanations</span></div></div>

  <section class="tf-section tf-wrap" id="how-it-works" aria-labelledby="how-title">
    <div class="tf-section-heading"><p class="tf-eyebrow">01 — HOW IT WORKS</p><h2 id="how-title">From “what is this?”<br>to “there’s the code.”</h2><p>Skip the tariff rabbit hole.<br>Start with what you already have.</p></div>
    <div class="tf-steps">
      <article><span class="tf-step-number">01&nbsp;<%= tf_arrow %></span><h3>Send us the product.</h3><p>Paste a link from your favourite shop. With a free account, you can also upload a photo or forward an order email.</p></article>
      <article><span class="tf-step-number">02&nbsp;<%= tf_arrow %></span><h3>We join the dots.</h3><p>Tariffik analyses the product details and finds a suggested classification using the official UK Trade Tariff.</p></article>
      <article><span class="tf-step-number">03 <span aria-hidden="true">✓</span></span><h3>Get a code you can check.</h3><p>See the suggested commodity code, a confidence rating, and the reasoning—so you can review it before declaring.</p></article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="tf-tools-section" id="features" aria-labelledby="tools-title"><div class="tf-wrap tf-section">
    <div class="tf-section-heading"><p class="tf-eyebrow">02 — A LITTLE MORE ORGANISED</p><h2 id="tools-title">Less admin.<br>More getting on with it.</h2><p>One place for your products,<br>orders, and that all-important code.</p></div>
    <div class="tf-tools-grid">
      <article class="tf-tool-feature"><span class="tf-tool-icon" aria-hidden="true">↳</span><div><p class="tf-eyebrow">YOUR IMPORTS, TOGETHER</p><h3>A home for every order.</h3><p>Forward your order confirmations. Keep products and suggested codes together, review your history, and export confirmed codes to CSV.</p><%= link_to safe_join([ "Get organised for free ", tf_arrow ]), new_user_registration_path(source: "home_orders"), class: "tf-text-link" %></div><div class="tf-order-preview" aria-hidden="true"><div><span>YOUR ORDERS</span><span>STATUS</span></div><div><strong>Cotton T-shirt</strong><span>Ready to review</span></div><div><strong>Ceramic coffee cup</strong><span>Ready to review</span></div><div><strong>Desk lamp</strong><span>Ready to review</span></div></div></article>
      <article class="tf-tool-small"><span class="tf-tool-icon" aria-hidden="true">◎</span><span class="tf-small-label">PHOTO LOOKUP · BETA</span><h3>Point. Snap. Classify.</h3><p>Got the product, but no link? Upload a photo and let Tariffik work out what it is.</p><%= link_to safe_join([ "Try photo lookup ", tf_arrow ]), user_signed_in? ? new_product_lookup_path(tab: "photo") : new_user_registration_path(source: "home_photo_card"), class: "tf-text-link" %></article>
      <article class="tf-tool-small tf-tool-mint"><span class="tf-tool-icon" aria-hidden="true">≡</span><span class="tf-small-label">THE REASONING INCLUDED</span><h3>More than a number.</h3><p>Understand why a code was suggested, with a confidence rating to help guide your review.</p><a href="#lookup" class="tf-text-link">Find your first code&nbsp;<%= tf_arrow %></a></article>
    </div>
  </div></section>

  <section class="tf-extension tf-wrap tf-section" aria-labelledby="extension-title">
    <div><p class="tf-eyebrow">03 — RIGHT WHERE YOU SHOP</p><h2 id="extension-title">New tab?<br>No need.</h2><p>Meet your shopping sidekick. The free Tariffik Chrome extension looks up commodity codes right on the product page.</p><ul class="tf-check-list"><li>Automatically reads product details</li><li>Opens neatly in your browser sidebar</li><li>Saves lookups to your Tariffik account</li></ul><a href="https://chromewebstore.google.com/detail/tariffik-commodity-code-l/gkjpgbgongkgdjfapjclandjhglnpmpn" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="tf-button tf-button-dark">Add to Chrome&nbsp;<%= tf_arrow %></a><span class="tf-extension-note">Free to install</span></div>
    <div class="tf-browser-preview"><div class="tf-browser-bar"><span aria-hidden="true">● ● ●</span><span>Your favourite shop / Tariffik</span><%= tf_arrow %></div><img src="/images/chrome-extension-sidepanel.png" alt="The Tariffik Chrome extension side panel suggesting commodity code 6109 10 0010 for an organic cotton T-shirt" loading="lazy" width="368" height="598"></div>
  </section>

  <section class="tf-mcp tf-wrap tf-section" id="mcp" aria-labelledby="mcp-title">
    <div>
      <p class="tf-eyebrow">04 — WORKING WITH AI</p>
      <h2 id="mcp-title">Ask Claude.<br>It asks Tariffik.</h2>
      <p>Connect Tariffik to Claude, or any assistant that speaks the Model Context Protocol. Then work the way you already do: point it at your order emails, and let it pull the product links and come back with the codes.</p>
      <ul class="tf-check-list">
        <li>Codes checked against the UK Trade Tariff, not guessed</li>
        <li>Lookups save to your account, ready for CSV export</li>
        <li>Included with a free account</li>
      </ul>
      <%= link_to user_signed_in? ? dashboard_path : new_user_registration_path(source: "home_mcp"), class: "tf-button tf-button-dark" do %><%= user_signed_in? ? "Connect it from your dashboard" : "Create a free account" %>&nbsp;<%= tf_arrow %><% end %>
      <span class="tf-extension-note">Works with Claude Code, Claude Desktop and Cursor</span>
    </div>
    <div class="tf-mcp-preview" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="tf-mcp-line tf-mcp-you"><span>You</span><p>Go through my order emails from last month and find the commodity codes.</p></div>
      <div class="tf-mcp-line tf-mcp-tool"><span>Tariffik</span><p><code>lookup_from_url</code> · allbirds.co.uk/products/wool-runner</p></div>
      <div class="tf-mcp-line tf-mcp-tool"><span>Tariffik</span><p><code>lookup_from_url</code> · uniqlo.com/uk/en/products/cotton-tee</p></div>
      <div class="tf-mcp-result"><p>Two codes found and saved.</p><div class="tf-mcp-code"><strong>6404</strong> <em>19</em> 9000 <span>Footwear, textile uppers</span></div><div class="tf-mcp-code"><strong>6109</strong> <em>10</em> 0010 <span>T-shirts, cotton</span></div></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="tf-pricing-section" id="pricing" aria-labelledby="pricing-title"><div class="tf-wrap tf-section">
    <div class="tf-section-heading"><p class="tf-eyebrow">05 — SIMPLE FROM THE START</p><h2 id="pricing-title">Small parcel.<br>Big shipment. You’re covered.</h2><p>Start free with an account.<br>Or put it to work for your business.</p></div>
    <div class="tf-pricing-grid">
      <article class="tf-plan tf-plan-featured"><div class="tf-plan-ribbon">A GOOD PLACE TO START</div><p class="tf-eyebrow">FREE ACCOUNT</p><h3>Make yourself at home.</h3><div class="tf-plan-amount">5 <span>lookups / month</span></div><p>Your everyday importing companion.<br>Free, every month.</p><ul class="tf-check-list"><li>Product links and photo lookup</li><li>Email lookups: forward an order, get the codes back</li><li>Connect Claude or another AI assistant over MCP</li><li>Saved lookup history and CSV export</li></ul><%= link_to new_user_registration_path(source: "home_pricing"), class: "tf-button tf-button-primary" do %>Create free account&nbsp;<%= tf_arrow %><% end %><small>No card needed</small></article>
      <article class="tf-plan"><p class="tf-eyebrow">BUSINESS</p><h3>Down to business.</h3><div class="tf-plan-amount tf-plan-custom">Let’s talk.</div><p>For bigger volumes and<br>your own connected workflows.</p><ul class="tf-check-list"><li>Everything in the free account</li><li>More lookups every month</li><li>API access and batch processing</li><li>Webhooks for your workflows</li></ul><a href="mailto:hello@tariffik.com?subject=Business%20Plan%20Enquiry" class="tf-button tf-button-outline">Get in touch&nbsp;<%= tf_arrow %></a><small>A plan to fit your business</small></article>
    </div>
  </div></section>

  <section class="tf-faq tf-wrap tf-section" aria-labelledby="faq-title"><div><p class="tf-eyebrow">A FEW GOOD QUESTIONS</p><h2 id="faq-title">Before you<br> send it.</h2></div><div class="tf-faq-list">
    <details><summary>What is a commodity code?<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><p>A commodity code classifies goods for customs. Tariffik helps you find a suggested code for a product, using its details and UK tariff data.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Do I need an account?<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><p>You can try one product-link lookup without signing up, to see how it works. A free account includes five lookups each month, photo and email lookups, saved history, and an MCP connection for Claude or another AI assistant.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Can I use a suggestion on my declaration?<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><p>Review the code and its explanation against your product before using it. Suggestions are a starting point; you remain responsible for your customs classification.</p></details>
    <details><summary>What if I don’t have a product link?<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><p>Create a free account to upload a product photo, or forward an order confirmation to your unique Tariffik email address.</p></details>
  </div></section>
  <section class="tf-final-cta"><div class="tf-wrap"><p class="tf-eyebrow">LESS GUESSING. MORE GOING.</p><h2>Your next import,<br>a little simpler.</h2><a href="#lookup" class="tf-button tf-button-primary">Let’s find that code&nbsp;<%= tf_arrow %></a><%= tf_arrow(classes: "tf-cta-mark") %></div></section>
</div>
